### HvacGuard telemetry API – open in Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code (REST Client)
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7180
@apiKey = change-me-dev-api-key

### Push a normal reading for unit 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "unitId": 1,
  "supplyAirTemperature": 18.2,
  "returnAirTemperature": 23.9,
  "relativeHumidity": 51.5,
  "fanSpeed": 78,
  "filterPressureDrop": 165
}

### Push a reading that violates the "supply air temperature high-high" rule
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "unitId": 1,
  "supplyAirTemperature": 26.4,
  "returnAirTemperature": 31.2,
  "relativeHumidity": 63,
  "fanSpeed": 77,
  "filterPressureDrop": 170
}

### Missing API key → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{ "unitId": 1, "supplyAirTemperature": 18, "returnAirTemperature": 24, "relativeHumidity": 50, "fanSpeed": 78, "filterPressureDrop": 150 }

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### OpenAPI document (Development only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json
